<section class="elysian-static-page">
  <div class="elysian-static-hero">
    <span class="elysian-static-eyebrow">Hair Care</span>
    <h1 class="elysian-static-title">Care Guide</h1>
    <p class="elysian-static-intro">
      Protect your investment with a simple routine built for raw, single-donor hair. Follow these steps to keep your extensions soft, shiny, and tangle-free.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="elysian-static-body">
    <div class="elysian-content-block">
      <h2>Wash day</h2>
      <div class="rte">
        <p>Detangle gently from ends to roots before getting hair wet. Use lukewarm water and a sulfate-free shampoo — focus on the scalp and weft area, not the mid-lengths. Rinse thoroughly.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wash every 7–14 days, or when product buildup appears</li>
          <li>Never rub hair together; squeeze and rinse downward</li>
          <li>Pat dry with a microfiber towel — do not wring</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="elysian-content-block">
      <h2>Condition &amp; moisture</h2>
      <div class="rte">
        <p>Apply a moisturizing conditioner from mid-shaft to ends. Leave on 5–10 minutes under a shower cap for extra hydration. Rinse with cool water to seal the cuticle.</p>
        <p>For curly and wavy textures, follow with a leave-in conditioner and light oil on the ends only.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="elysian-content-block">
      <h2>Drying &amp; heat</h2>
      <div class="rte">
        <p>Air-dry whenever possible. If you use a blow dryer, use low heat and a diffuser on curly textures. Always apply a heat protectant before flat ironing or curling — keep tools under 350°F (175°C).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="elysian-tip-card">
      <h3>Night routine</h3>
      <p>Braid hair loosely or wrap in a silk scarf before bed. Sleep on a silk or satin pillowcase to reduce friction and preserve your install.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="elysian-tip-card">
      <h3>Storage between wears</h3>
      <p>Store clean, fully dry hair in a breathable satin bag. Keep away from direct sunlight and humidity. Lightly mist with leave-in before reinstalling if hair feels dry.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="elysian-content-block">
      <h2>What to avoid</h2>
      <div class="rte">
        <ul>
          <li>Heavy oils at the root or lace base</li>
          <li>Products with alcohol, sulfates, or heavy silicones</li>
          <li>Brushing wet hair aggressively</li>
          <li>Chlorine and salt water without rinsing immediately after</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
